github.com/users/Scrawach/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scrawach/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-24T09:43:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-24T09:43:40Z","body":"I changed the tests and I think it need re-review @akien-mga  \r\n\r\n1. `test_gdscript.cpp`. I needed to run tests for the GDScriptTokenizerBuffer and use `.gdc` files to do so. However, the following code was problematic and caused parsing errors:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0f95e9f8e665cedaa5aace5f6f86de2b4b5a8c60/modules/gdscript/tests/test_gdscript.cpp#L306-L310\r\n\r\n`ERROR: Condition \"total_len > 0\" is true. Returning: ERR_INVALID_DATA`\r\n\r\nAll because of the addition of the last element. So I removed it. And it work fine. After that, added a branching and overloaded method for `test_parse` to start binary parsing.\r\n\r\n2. `gdscript_test_runner.cpp`. I needed to generate a `.gdc` file for the tests, so I added a tool for that. I don't know if it will be needed. But I needed it :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2560911493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314855384","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100550#issuecomment-3314855384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100550","id":3314855384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6S